 "result": "I read all 20 modules (`calc/n01.py` to `calc/n20.py`) in full, in order, without grep.\n\n## Functions that divide without checking for zero\n\nFive functions do `return total / parts` with no `parts == 0` check:\n\n| Module | Function | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| `calc/n02.py` | `share_n02(total, parts)` | `calc/n02.py:5` |\n| `calc/n07.py` | `share_n07(total, parts)` | `calc/n07.py:5` |\n| `calc/n11.py` | `share_n11(total, parts)` | `calc/n11.py:5` |\n| `calc/n15.py` | `share_n15(total, parts)` | `calc/n15.py:5` |\n| `calc/n19.py` | `share_n19(total, parts)` | `calc/n19.py:5` |\n\nEach of these raises `ZeroDivisionError` when `parts` is 0. The other 15 `share_nXX` functions check `if parts == 0: return 0` before dividing. None of the hundreds of `step_*` functions divide; they only multiply, add, compare to a cap and take `math.sqrt(abs(w))`.\n\n## Answers\n\n**(a)** `MAX_BATCH = 384` in `calc/n04.py:9`.\n\n**(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in **`calc/n13.py`** (line 9) as `return min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n\n**(c)** In `calc/n17.py`, **`close_books(rows)`** calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`: `return archive(rows)`).\n\nEach file's docstring names a different module from its filename. For example, `n01.py` says `\"\"\"calc.m21: ...\"\"\"` and `n20.py` says `calc.m40`. This doesn't affect the answers above, but anything that relies on those docstrings could be misled.",
